Shaderboard bindings of type `shaderboard:scoreboard_objective` can now pass a sorted array of scores to post-effect shaders.

Example JSON:
```json
{
	"uniform_name": "u_SortedScoresAZ",
	"type": "shaderboard:scoreboard_objective",
	"objective": "example_1",
	"target":
	{
		"type": "array",
		"count": 16,
		"include_hidden": true,
		"sort": [
			{ "by": "name", "order": "ascending" }
		],
		"offset": 0
	}
}
```

Example GLSL:
```glsl
layout(std140) uniform u_SortedScoresAZ {
	int sortedScores[16];
};
```

This update brings in even more bindings that give post-effect shaders more information about the game environment.

A proper documentation is planned once I implemnet and release all the features I have planned (which I have not yet done).

### Configuration system
This mod now has a dedicated configuration file with currently only one configurable property. To configure it, create the following file: `[profile_dir]/config/shaderboard.json`, and inside, write the following baseline JSON:
```json
{
	"client-logLoadingWarnings": true
}
```
More info will be made available once I finally write a proper documentation.

### `shaderboard:local_player_attribute`
Exposes the entity attribute system to post-effect shaders. Please note that some attributes are entirely server-sided and thus reading them from client-sided post-effect shaders may produce unreliable results.

Example JSON:
```json
{
	"uniform_name": "u_MyChonkiness",
	"type": "shaderboard:local_player_attribute"
	"attribute": "minecraft:scale"
}
```
Example GLSL:
```glsl
layout(std140) uniform u_MyChonkiness {
	float baseValue;
	float value;
};
```

### `shaderboard:local_player_status_effect`
Lets post-effect shaders know if the local player has a specific status effect alongside how long it lasts and of what amplifier.  
When `duration` reads `0` then the status effect is not present. When `duration` reads `-1`, then the status effect's duration is infinite. When `duration` is greater than 0, then the effect is present and lasts for a given amount of time.

Example JSON:
```json
{
	"uniform_name": "u_MyNightVision",
	"type": "shaderboard:local_player_status_effect"
	"effect": "minecraft:night_vision"
}
```
Example GLSL:
```glsl
layout(std140) uniform u_MyNightVision {
	int duration; //can be -1, and -1 means "infinite duration"
	int amplifier;
	int isInfinite; //0 = finite, 1 = infinite duration.
};
```

### `shaderboard:local_player_motion_state`
Gives post-effect shaders general information about what the local player's character is currently doing movement-wise.

Example JSON:
```json
{
	"uniform_name": "u_MyMoves",
	"type": "shaderboard:local_player_motion_state"
}
```
Example GLSL:
```glsl
layout(std140) uniform u_MyMoves {
	//these are integers posing as booleans; 0 = no, 1 = yes.
	int isOnGround;
	int isCrouching;
	int isSprinting;
	int isSwimming;
	int isUnderwater;
	int isFlying;
	int isGliding;
	int isRiding;
};
```

This update brings in more bindings that give post-effect shaders more information about the game environment, this time about the "local player" (aka the player character one plays as).

To keep things organized, I plan on writing a detailed documentation soon.

### `shaderboard:local_player_health`
Provides information about the local player's health (in half-heart units), max health, and absorption.

Example JSON:
```json
{
	"uniform_name": "u_MyHealth",
	"type": "shaderboard:local_player_health"
}
```
Example GLSL:
```glsl
layout(std140) uniform u_MyHealth {
	float health;
	float maxHealth;
	float absorption;
};
```

